WEBVTT

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:07.010
Once again, we're wrapping up 
at the very last second.

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.880
I'm glad we made it in time, though!

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.400
Excuse me?

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.380
Not being able to record the voice-overs 
means we didn't make it in time.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:15.960
True...

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.030
We'll have to do the dubbing live.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:21.650
All thanks to a certain someone 
and their late animation.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.560
I can go ahead and record the performance,

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.830
but there's a lot of echo 
in the auditorium...

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:30.370
I don't know if it'll be good 
enough to use on the DVDs.

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:33.380
I'm still worried about how Onocchy's 
reads are gonna turn out.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.970
I'll go ahead and run it.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:01.610
What do you think, Asakusa?

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.230
You haven't balanced it yet, right?

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.500
Right. As it stands, only the timing is done.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.510
Although I was making adjustments 
while it was playing...

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:13.620
About the music in cut 6... 
Does it seem out of sync to you?

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:15.680
Probably because the action 
on screen doesn't happen

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.660
until after the music peaks.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:19.010
We could try delaying it.

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:21.580
You mean offsetting it even 
more from the action?

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:23.350
Wouldn't that mess with the big hit?

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:24.390
Let's see.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.910
I'm not sure why, but I think that's better!

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:36.610
The music is setting the tone before 
the action, and leading the audience along!

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:40.170
There were a few spots where the music 
and the action didn't have the right tone,

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:43.140
where I was thinking we 
could use different tracks.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:47.260
For cut 150 and 82...

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.210
If we use the music from cut 24,

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:51.120
we can create a motif linking 
the different scenes.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:52.070
What do you think?

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:54.420
Sounds like it might work. Let me try it.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:58.930
Something about the music for
 cut 86 doesn't sit right with me.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:04.390
What if we dropped 
the music for that part?

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.190
You mean to put an emphasis 
on the sound effects from 79?

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:14.940
The animation is amazing for that part.
 So by subtracting the music...

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.290
So cool!

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.500
That makes the scene really stand out!

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.230
You're some kind of music master, Asakusa!

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.800
We are so sorry.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.140
Who would've thought production 
would end up canceled

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:48.980
because the director and screenwriter 
tried to murder a producer?

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:48.980
<b>Film Director Tomo Komatsu Arrested for Attempted Murder</b>

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:48.980
<b>Komatsu's arrest</b>

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:48.980
<b>m 280 111 l 377 161 478 71 385 28</b>

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:48.980
<b></b>On the 19th in Nishi-Azabu, Tokyo,
a movie director was arrested for 
attempting to kill a movie producer.
with a katana.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:48.980
<b>m 305 254 l 387 300 571 115 501 78</b>

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:48.980
<b></b>Police believe that Komatsu and an accomplice attempted to slice open
the stomach of movie producer Jubei Honda (52). Mr. Honda is in
 critical condition, but Mr. Komatsu denies the allegations stating he does
 not recall what happened.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:52.920
It was supposed to be your first time 
onscreen together in sixteen years, too.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.580
It's not that big a deal, right?

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:57.670
Yeah. To be honest, we kind of saw this coming.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:01.070
We are so sorry!

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:05.280
We can actually visit our daughter's 
culture festival, thanks to this.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.820
We were onscreen together sixteen years ago,

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.290
but we've never been to her cultural festival.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:14.020
We haven't exactly been the most... 
present of parents for her.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.430
Being able to improvise a kettle 
stand from pegs like this...

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:44.070
Sometimes, I do impress myself.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:51.460
Well, here's to the culture 
festival being a success!

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.540
Let's eat!

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.020
Unlike last time,

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.350
we're going to need to attract an 
audience for today's screening.

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:59.580
I definitely want lots of people to watch it!

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:00.810
That's part of it,

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:02.980
but our primary objective 
today is to score preorders

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:05.130
for the DVD release after 
the screening today.

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:06.230
Again with the money...

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:08.060
And that's why we need an audience.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:12.140
First, since it's summer, we'll need to 
make sure our auditorium is nice and cool.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:13.660
Good idea.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:17.020
But I hear the HVAC club are 
lackeys of the student council.

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:20.110
It'll be fine. I've got 
what I need to negotiate.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:22.860
But more important than even that...

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:27.420
is the involvement of the popular 
amateur model Tsubame Mizusaki,

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:30.630
and how much we can 
put her out in front of this.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:32.140
Whoa! Hang on!

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:34.750
That makes it sounds like the anime 
would be playing second fiddle

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.330
to Tsubame Mizusaki!

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.890
What're you talking about?

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:40.680
We're using you along with 
air-conditioning to get people

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.670
to pay attention to the anime,

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:45.680
not the other way around. Right?

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:48.600
I-I guess, but...

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.850
We're going to win over the people who 
came to see you with the anime's quality.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:55.910
Which we can't do if they won't show up.

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:59.070
And if the short is good enough, 
they're bound to preorder the DVD.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:00.520
That's a lot of extra responsibility..

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:05.430
We've got a big spotlight that'll 
allow us to draw plenty of attention.

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:08.740
We need to use that to our 
advantage as much as possible.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.270
Whether we like it or not,

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:14.460
if it benefits our production situation 
in the long run, we need to do it.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:15.310
I'm kinda worried

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:17.820
my parents might find out if 
I draw too much attention, though.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:20.550
Oh, right, if your parents find out...

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:21.840
Huh? Asakusa...

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:24.220
You're holding your chopsticks kind of weird.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.370
You can actually grab stuff like that?!

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:39.350
I think I'll be our poster girl after all.

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:42.700
My parents found out I didn't go home today.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:44.440
You didn't tell them?

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.420
If they knew I was working 
on the culture festival,

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:47.780
they'd want to know specifics...

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:52.240
And they just told me... that they're coming.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.830
Wh-What?!

00:05:55.150 --> 00:06:00.330
But if they find out, you won't be 
able to make anime anymore, Mizusaki!

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:06.840
<b><i>Episode 8       The Grand Shibahama Festival!</i></b>

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.210
<b><i>Keep</i></b>

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:03.560
<b><i>Your</i></b>

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.130
<b><i>Hands</i></b>

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:08.510
<b><i>Off</i></b>

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:19.500
<b><i>Keep Your Hands Off Eizouken!</i></b>

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:27.710
<b><i>Keep Your Hands Off Eizouken!</i></b>

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:44.480
Are you sure about this, Mizusaki?

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:48.450
I don't care if they find out anymore! 
My family situation can suck it!

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:52.310
If they're coming, then bring 'em on!
 I'll give them a real eyeful!

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:54.250
Besides, if I can't bring in 
a crowd for this screening,

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:55.460
we're at a dead end anyway!

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:58.370
Hell yeah! You'll have our 
full support as backup!

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.280
For once, we're gonna 
tackle things with spirit!

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:04.370
Spirit, spirit, spirit, go!

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:08.440
We've already lost the chance 
to form a line, though...

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.420
It's like everyone's putting 
on a spirited show.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.420
Our electromagnetic amoeba!

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.420
<b>Electro-
magnetic
 Amoeba</b>

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.420
<b>Accessibility 
Research Club</b>

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:13.070
<i>Pi Research Club 
~The Beauty of Pi~ 
Pi Is Great!</i>

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.220
<b>Rap Club</b>

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.220
<b>Rakuda</b>

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.840
I'm the best there is! No. 1 in the biz!

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:15.970
<b>Shortwave Radio Research Club!
Shortwave radio tournament coming up on the East Tower roof</b>

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:18.510
<b>Oden Club</b>

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:18.510
<b>Shaved Ice Club</b>

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:18.510
Hot, hot, hot! That radish is too...

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:18.510
Anyone want some shaved ice?

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:19.280
<b>Shingeki Theater Research Club 
 We will be performing in Auditorium 3!!</b>

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:21.180
<b>Presented by the Robot Study Club Featuring the Eizouken
SHIBA8 VS The Pistol Crabtle
The Great Shibahama Festival!
Including an appearance by the famous model
Tsubame Mizusaki

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:23.280
We're the eizouken! Please check us out!

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:26.130
Tsubame Mizusaki has worked on an anime—

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:26.730
Please come by!

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:27.270
We've got anime!

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:31.030
Tsubame Mizusaki will be appearing at—

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:35.410
Even the people who'd come to see 
you won't notice us at this rate.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:37.870
Thank you for your service!

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.830
<b>Tsubame Mizusaki</b>

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:41.850
The robot club?

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:43.780
The prep took longer than anticipated.

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:53.880
<b>Tsubame Mizusaki! We're Launching a Rocket Before the Robot Anime Screening!</b>

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:52.040
Hey, what's that?

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:53.880
What the...

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:58.600
Count down along with us!

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:00.720
Ten! Nine!

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:04.270
Eight! Seven! Six! Five!

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:06.850
<b>Tsubame Mizusaki! We're Launching a Rocket Before the Robot Anime Screening!</b>

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:08.110
Four! Three! Two! One!

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:10.110
Fire!

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:18.440
A robot anime featuring Tsubame Mizusaki

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.620
will be screening in Auditorium No. 1!

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:23.700
I made an anime! Come check it out!

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.210
I'll also be greeting the audience!

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:27.980
Wait, isn't that...

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:27.980
It's really her!

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:29.220
Tsubame Mizusaki!

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:33.970
She's so cute!

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:35.220
Dang...

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.840
Man, celebs have it easy.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.400
I thought there was a ban on megaphones?

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.200
Three-Star
Restaurant

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:41.680
It's nice and cool inside! Care to join us?

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:41.680
So she gets away with it because she's famous?

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:45.180
Let's leave this to Mizusaki 
and the robot club.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:47.270
We need to cover the rest of the campus.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:48.600
Roger!

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:58.570
What about twenty-two?

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:04.080
Is that number your idea of a joke? 
Because I'm not here for comedy.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:05.970
You'd better watch your mouth.

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:06.730
Who do you think you are?

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:07.540
Wait.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:11.570
How about it? Twenty-one suit you better?

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:12.850
Eighteen.

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:14.540
Twenty.

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:15.980
Sixteen, then.

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:16.880
Nineteen!

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:18.950
I said sixteen.

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:23.510
You dirty, rotten...

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.520
<b>Auditorium 1</b>

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:38.990
<b>Fight for every degree°</b>

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:30.820
We've got a deal, then.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:33.770
President, why?!

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:35.160
It's ecologically criminal!

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.420
And if the student council 
finds out, we'll be in huge trouble!

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:38.990
You're all guilty, too!

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:45.820
If these pictures get out, we're done for!

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:50.250
Damn it! She's a monster! A devil!

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:54.010
Autographs will be available 
at the screening!

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:56.960
This is a handshake-only promotion!

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:59.980
Head to the auditorium if you want more!

00:10:57.830 --> 00:10:59.980
Please don't crowd together!

00:11:00.270 --> 00:11:01.980
Proceed into school grounds.

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:05.220
The use of megaphones and aerial 
accoutrements is forbidden!

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:07.540
What were you going to do if you 
hit someone with that rocket?!

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:11.070
Mizusaki of the eizouken, you're under
 arrest as the ringleader!

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:12.820
This is a promotion by the robot club!

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:14.730
The responsibility lies with us!

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:18.030
Everyone, head on over to 
Auditorium No. 1 and shake hands with me!

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:20.230
Mizusaki...

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:25.560
Here. Kanamori gave the order.

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:28.650
We're all going to protect you, so don't worry.

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:30.210
Thank you...

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:34.080
Anything for the robot anime's screening.

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:37.970
Where's Mizusaki?

00:11:37.970 --> 00:11:39.580
I don't know.

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:42.800
You're in the robot club, 
but I don't see any cardboard.

00:11:47.590 --> 00:11:48.570
There!

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:55.810
<i>Mizusaki, excellent work.</i>

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:57.940
<i>Now you just need to make 
it to the auditorium.</i>

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:59.230
Is this gonna work?!

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:01.820
Keep going ahead. I'll direct you.

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:04.590
Anyone in a cardboard robot is on our side.

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:06.110
Watch out for the security club.

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:08.830
<i>Get down.</i>

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:16.330
<b>Udon</b>

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:16.330
<b>Woodworking
Club</b>

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:16.330
<b>Karaage
Ramen</b>

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:14.140
<i>Head down those stairs.</i>

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:26.090
<b>Danger</b>

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:18.470
<i>Stop!</i>

00:12:21.190 --> 00:12:24.830
<i>Okay. Keep going, and then head 
into the hall on your left.</i>

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:27.140
I've got her!

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:30.060
We've apprehended a robot.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.600
Get that one, too!

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:34.100
We've caught a robot we believe to be Mizusaki.

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:36.440
We've also caught one of the Mizusaki robots.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:37.440
Same here.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:39.440
We've spotted a crowd of them!

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.100
<i>We'll move to apprehend them—</i>

00:12:39.850 --> 00:12:41.100
<i>We've restrained one.</i>

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:41.820
<i>Got another one here.</i>

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:42.490
<i>Should we pursue?</i>

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.450
How many people are even in the eizouken?!

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:45.900
Catch them all!

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:47.310
You're under arrest!

