They're not coming off!

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:21.470
Some of them might not be students.

00:13:21.470 --> 00:13:23.430
Don't get too rough.

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:26.610
He's getting away! After him!

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:32.950
My soul, dadada! A body of iron, dadada!

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:39.170
An invincible body with a steel 
heart fighting to the end, dadada!

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:43.670
Dun dun dun dun, 
machines have no tears to shed!

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:43.670
Ono... he's powering up!

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:47.930
But you can see the passion 
welling up inside!

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:46.070
We'll deal with them later!

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:47.930
Go, Ono!

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:49.720
Passion!

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:51.300
Boy, that takes me back.

00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:52.470
So cool!

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:56.730
<b>Robot anime screening in Auditorium No. 1!
 With Tsubame Mizusaki!</b>

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:54.980
Huh, an anime screening?

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:55.800
Let's check it out!

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:56.740
Sounds good.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:58.810
<b>Zip Line</b>

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:13.540
<b>Z       I       P       L         I        NE</b>

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:12.610
Here he comes!

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:13.540
Welcome!

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:18.670
Switch: Super Wing!

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:23.170
Easy does it!

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:30.450
<b>Robot anime screening featuring Tsubame Mizusaki!</b>

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:31.480
What the heck?

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:32.430
What's his deal?

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:34.180
Holy moly!

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:42.140
Touchdown!

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:46.160
I'm gonna check your show out!

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:47.320
Good luck!

00:14:59.530 --> 00:15:01.330
That's a big crowd!

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:03.010
Mission accomplished.

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:04.150
Where's Asakusa?

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:06.180
She's still passing out 
fliers near the entrance.

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:08.000
She should be on her way back in.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:10.180
Mizusaki! We need you 
standing by at stage left.

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:13.430
I did it... I've done it!

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:16.090
I did it!

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:17.680
You're not done yet.

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:20.060
The show's about to start!

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.370
<b>Presented by the Robot Study Club Featuring the Eizouken
SHIBA8 VS The Pistol Crabtle
The Great Shibahama Festival!
Including an appearance by the famous model
Tsubame Mizusaki

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:24.160
I remember you!

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:25.190
Men in black!

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.230
Get back here!

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:28.070
Hang on a sec.

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:33.420
The robot club has holed up
 inside Auditorium No. 1.

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:34.780
Should we breach?

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:37.160
We can't take them in if 
they're inside the venue.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:39.290
Nail them as soon as they set foot outside!

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:41.790
Oh crap! Oh crap! Oh crap!

00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:45.110
I just handed a flier to some men 
in black and Mizusaki's parents!

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:47.630
They're already here.

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:55.270
It's almost time.

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:03.130
The robot study club will now 
begin the screening of its anime!

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.730
This should be good!

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:10.250
It's Tsubame Mizusaki!

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:11.770
Tsubame!

00:16:11.770 --> 00:16:13.630
There she is!

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:19.790
We're so sorry. We tried to stop her, but...

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:23.040
They did?

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:27.250
It was my idea. I wanted to get 
Tsubame's mind off of anime.

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:30.950
You wanted her to be an actress, remember?

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:42.230
I am really excited for this.

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:43.360
Now!

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:44.480
Wait, it's not—

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:46.810
Please enjoy!

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:09.920
Hey, that's really Shibahama! Cool!

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:12.880
Look at them eat!

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:15.340
Why so much crab?

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:18.410
Look at that...

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:25.770
Vibrations have been detected 
in the underground pit.

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:29.300
<i>A monster resembling a crab has appeared.</i>

00:17:29.300 --> 00:17:31.780
<i>I repeat, a monster resembling 
a crab has appeared...</i>

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:40.330
Open it up... Easy does it...

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:47.790
<b>Preparing Launch</b>

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:48.580
<b>Launching</b>

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:55.630
Head directly to the subterranean waterway.

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:59.090
<i>The target is on a slow and steady 
course through the underground.</i>

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:05.930
Recoil starter!

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:32.460
That running...

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:33.550
It's Tsubame.

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:37.190
A cooling fan is down, and the movement 
software isn't coming online!

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:39.710
Wh-What?! Manual control?!

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:16.530
You remember how Tsubame's 
always been good at dancing?

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:18.730
She'd mimic what she saw on TV.

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:22.550
Yeah. She used to imitate 
how her grandma moved, too.

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:24.500
And that bit before...

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:34.390
She was always analyzing and 
repeating things she saw.

00:19:34.390 --> 00:19:36.060
I always thought it was brilliant.

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:44.660
But at some point...

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:47.900
She started having more fun 
recreating the movements

00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:50.930
she saw with art, rather than with her body.

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:55.960
I think her real talent is her eye for detail.

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:03.720
And even without the help of their parents...

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.850
Kids will still grow up.

00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:10.940
There's real ingenuity to all this.

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:14.600
I've been on her case about 
becoming an actress, but...

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:20.610
Tsubame is already a fine performer.

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:44.610
<b>Sponsor
Robot Study Club</b>

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:50.550
Tsubame!

00:20:51.490 --> 00:20:52.550
Tsubame!

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:57.900
<b>Tsubame Mizusaki Autograph Session</b>

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:57.900
Preorder your DVD now and you'll get a bonus!

00:20:58.460 --> 00:21:02.150
<u>Candid Photos</u> of Animator <b>Tsubame Mizusaki</b>

00:20:58.860 --> 00:20:59.850
Want!

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:02.150
I gotta get that bonus!

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:04.130
Please line up!

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:05.800
An invincible body and a steel heart!

00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:07.160
You don't get in line, you don't get the bonus!

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:08.920
That was amazing!

00:21:08.920 --> 00:21:10.980
Really? Thank you so much!

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:14.930
Thanks for coming by!

00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:18.680
We'll take it from here.

00:21:18.680 --> 00:21:22.420
Head out the back and grab 
us some lunch, please.

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:24.460
Yeah! Thanks.

00:21:24.460 --> 00:21:27.460
We've got plenty to go around.

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:31.680
And if you preorder now, you can get an 
autographed picture of Tsubame Mizusaki!

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:34.970
Go ahead and put down your name and 
address on the form while you're in line.

00:21:34.970 --> 00:21:36.310
Cash only.

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:38.940
<b>Yakisoba</b>

00:21:37.820 --> 00:21:38.940
Four, please.

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:40.950
That'll be 1,600 yen.

00:21:42.310 --> 00:21:43.690
Let me get that.

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:45.950
<b>Yakisoba</b>

00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:45.070
Hey.

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:55.550
Say... have you ever been 
satisfied with a performance?

00:21:57.620 --> 00:21:59.460
I haven't.

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:00.670
Me neither.

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:01.930
I see.

00:22:03.980 --> 00:22:05.470
I realized something working on it.

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:11.340
That to me, life is about 
working on stuff like this.

00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:15.850
And there's nothing I can do about that, now.

00:22:18.940 --> 00:22:20.630
I need to take this to the others!

00:22:24.970 --> 00:22:27.110
What did you think of my animation?

00:22:29.410 --> 00:22:32.260
Real explosions give off a different impression.

00:22:32.260 --> 00:22:33.870
And the way they held those chopsticks...

00:22:33.870 --> 00:22:37.000
You could've told me sooner! 
I didn't find out until this morning!

00:22:37.810 --> 00:22:40.790
But... it was some fine acting.

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:47.300
Just what I'd expect from a couple 
of actors. You know what to look for!

00:22:54.610 --> 00:22:55.690
Sorry about the wait!

00:22:55.690 --> 00:22:56.560
Mizusaki!

00:22:57.170 --> 00:22:59.260
There were a ton of preorders for the DVDs.

00:22:59.260 --> 00:23:01.570
And we ran out of all the 
pictures we had prepared.

00:23:02.590 --> 00:23:05.910
Despite the reception, I feel like I'm 
only satisfied with 20% of what we did.

00:23:05.910 --> 00:23:07.320
Again?

00:23:07.980 --> 00:23:11.380
It might've been more impressive 
with more long shots...

00:23:11.380 --> 00:23:13.000
And a more detailed 
background during the scene

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:16.950
with the wall collapsing would've 
added to the sense of scale—

00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:21.140
Are you Tsubame's friends?

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:25.210
N-No, ma'am...

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:27.310
We're her comrades!

00:24:55.970 --> 00:25:00.250
<b>Illustration by: Shoko Takahata</b>
